\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s10 \li1209 \fi-1007 \ri1007 \ql Class Description\
\fs14\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 An NSThread object controls a thread of execution. Use NSThread when you want to have an Objective-C message run in its own thread of execution or if you need to terminate or delay the current thread. \
\fs14\
\fs28 A \i thread\i0  is an executable unit. A \i task\i0  is made up of one or more threads. Each thread has its own execution stack and is capable of independent input/output. All threads share the virtual memory address space and communication rights of their task. When a thread is started, it is \i detached\i0  from its initiating thread. The new thread runs independently. That is, the initiating thread does not know the new thread\'27s state.\
\fs14\
\fs28 To have an Objective-C message run in its own thread of execution, send the message \b detachNewThreadSelector:toTarget:withObject:\b0  to the NSThread class object. This method detaches a new thread from the current thread, and the specified target executes the specified method in that thread. When the target has finished executing the method, the thread exits. \
\fs14\
\fs28 When you use \b detachNewThreadSelector:toTarget:withObject:\b0 , your application becomes multithreaded. At any time you can send \b isMultiThreaded\b0  to find out if the application is multithreaded, that is, if a thread was ever detached from the main thread. \b isMultiThreaded\b0  returns YES even if the detached thread has completed execution. \
\fs14\
\pard \s46 \li2310 \fi-798 \ri1007 \ql \tx2308 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 Note:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 Do not interchange the use of the \b cthreads\b0  functions and NSThread objects within an application. In particular, do not use \b cthread_fork()\b0  to create a thread that executes an Objective-C message. \b isMultiThreaded\b0  returns YES only if \b detachNewThreadSelector:toTarget:withObject:\b0  was used to create the thread.\
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 If you need to terminate the current thread, send the \b exit\b0  message to the NSThread class object. Similarly, you send the \b sleepUntilDate:\b0  message to the NSThread class object to block the current thread for a period of time. \
\fs14\
